.SH NOTES
.BR \%bkgrnd ","
.BR \%bkgrndset ","
and
.B \%getbkgrnd
may be implemented as macros.
.PP
Unlike their counterparts in the non-wide-character configuration of
.IR \%ncurses ","
.B \%getbkgrnd
and
.B \%wgetbkgrnd
store the background character in a modifiable
.I \%cchar_t
parameter,
rather than supplying it as the return value.
